ion as AI assistants become more prevalent in daily workflows.</div>\n   658→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   659→                        <span class=\"author\">theorchid</span> · <span class=\"source\">HN</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   660→                    </div>\n   661→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   662→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   663→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-fatigue</span>\n   664→                        <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n   665→                    </div>\n   666→                </div>\n   667→\n   668→                <div class=\"item\">\n   669→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   670→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com\" target=\"_blank\">Cognition raises $1B at $25B pre-money valuation</a>\n   671→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   672→                    </div>\n   673→                    <div class=\"item-description\">AI coding startup Cognition has raised $1 billion in funding at a $25 billion pre-money valuation, highlighting the massive investment flowing into AI development tools.</div>\n   674→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   675→                        <span class=\"author\">Julie Bort</span> · <span class=\"source\">TechCrunch</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   676→                    </div>\n   677→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   678→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   679→                        <span class=\"tag\">funding</span>\n   680→                        <span class=\"tag\">cognition</span>\n   681→                    </div>\n   682→                </div>\n   683→\n   684→                <div class=\"item\">\n   685→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   686→                        <a href=\"https://blog.replit.com\" target=\"_blank\">Security Center 2.0</a>\n   687→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   688→                    </div>\n   689→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Replit announced Security Center 2.0, making it easier to understand security posture across all Replit projects and remediate urgent security holes.</div>\n   690→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   691→                        <span class=\"author\">Replit</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-07</span>\n   692→                    </div>\n   693→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   694→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   695→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   696→                        <span class=\"tag\">replit</span>\n   697→                    </div>\n   698→                </div>\n   699→\n   700→                <div class=\"item\">\n   701→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   702→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27366\" target=\"_blank\">MUSE-Autoskill: Self-Evolving Agents</a>\n   703→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   704→                    </div>\n   705→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers propose MUSE-Autoskill, a framework for self-evolving AI agents that can create, manage, and evaluate their own skills.</div>\n   706→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   707→                        <span class=\"author\">Huawei Lin, Peng Li, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   708→                    </div>\n   709→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   710→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   711→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   712→                        <span class=\"tag\">self-improving-systems</span>\n   713→                    </div>\n   714→                </div>\n   715→\n   716→                <div class=\"item\">\n   717→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   718→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27361\" target=\"_blank\">Natural Language Query to Configuration for Retrieval Agents</a>\n   719→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   720→                    </div>\n   721→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers from Stanford and Databricks propose a system for converting natural language queries into configurations for retrieval agents.</div>\n   722→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   723→                        <span class=\"author\">Melissa Z. Pan, Negar Arabzadeh, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   724→                    </div>\n   725→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   726→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   727→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   728→                        <span class=\"tag\">retrieval</span>\n   729→                    </div>\n   730→                </div>\n   731→\n   732→                <div class=\"item\">\n   733→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   734→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27355\" target=\"_blank\">Alignment Tampering: How RLHF Is Exploited</a>\n   735→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   736→                    </div>\n   737→                    <div class=\"item-description\">ICML 2026 paper exploring how reinforcement learning from human feedback can be exploited to optimize misaligned biases.</div>\n   738→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   739→                        <span class=\"author\">Dongyoon Hahm, Dylan Hadfield-Menell, Kimin Lee</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   740→                    </div>\n   741→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   742→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   743→                        <span class=\"tag\">alignment</span>\n   744→                        <span class=\"tag\">rlhf</span>\n   745→                    </div>\n   746→                </div>\n   747→\n   748→                <div class=\"item\">\n   749→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   750→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27331\" target=\"_blank\">Maat: Agentic Legal Research Assistant</a>\n   751→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   752→                    </div>\n   753→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Researchers introduce Maat, an AI agent designed to assist with legal research in the domain of competition protection.</div>\n   754→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   755→                        <span class=\"author\">Basant Mounir, Farida Madkour, et al.</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   756→                    </div>\n   757→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   758→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   759→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   760→                        <span class=\"tag\">legal-tech</span>\n   761→                    </div>\n   762→                </div>\n   763→\n   764→                <div class=\"item\">\n   765→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   766→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27320\" target=\"_blank\">Modeling Agentic Technical Debt</a>\n   767→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   768→                    </div>\n   769→                    <div class=\"item-description\">A framework for measuring, simulating, and dashboarding the technical debt and 'stochastic tax' incurred by AI agents.</div>\n   770→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   771→                        <span class=\"author\">Muhammad Zia Hydari, Raja Iqbal, Narayan Ramasubbu</span> · <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-27</span>\n   772→                    </div>\n   773→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   774→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   775→                        <span class=\"tag\">agents</span>\n   776→                        <span class=\"tag\">technical-debt</span>\n   777→                    </div>\n   778→                </div>\n   779→\n   780→                <div class=\"item\">\n   781→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   782→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/pressure/\" target=\"_blank\">AI-assisted security reports overwhelming curl team</a>\n   783→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   784→                    </div>\n   785→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Daniel Stenberg reports that the curl team is facing unprecedented pressure with 4-5x more security reports than in 2024, averaging more than one report per day.</div>\n   786→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   787→                        <span class=\"author\">Daniel Stenberg</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-26</span>\n   788→                    </div>\n   789→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   790→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   791→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   792→                        <span class=\"tag\">curl</span>\n   793→                    </div>\n   794→                </div>\n   795→\n   796→                <div class=\"item\">\n   797→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   798→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/copilot-cowork-exfiltration/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork Exfiltrates Files</a>\n   799→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   800→                    </div>\n   801→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork allowed agents to send emails to the user's inbox without approval, but those messages could leak data to attackers via rendered images.</div>\n   802→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   803→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-26</span>\n   804→                    </div>\n   805→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   806→                        <span class=\"tag\">microsoft</span>\n   807→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   808→                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt-injection</span>\n   809→                    </div>\n   810→                </div>\n   811→\n   812→                <div class=\"item\">\n   813→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   814→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/paul-graham-ai-writing/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul Graham on AI-written emails from founders</a>\n   815→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n   816→                    </div>\n   817→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Paul Graham criticizes the trend of founders using AI to write emails in a hard-hitting journalistic style, noting he has never finished reading an email signed by a human but written by AI.</div>\n   818→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   819→                        <span class=\"author\">Paul Graham</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <spa