       <div class=\"item-description\">Armin Ronacher expresses frustration with people submitting issues not in their own voice - problems thrown into an LLM that reworded them into messes of inaccurate conclusions.</div>\n   850→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   851→                        <span class=\"author\">Armin Ronacher</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-24</span>\n   852→                    </div>\n   853→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   854→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   855→                        <span class=\"tag\">github-issues</span>\n   856→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   857→                    </div>\n   858→                </div>\n   859→\n   860→                <div class=\"item\">\n   861→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   862→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/ftc-active-listening/\" target=\"_blank\">FTC Settles Charges Over Deceptive 'Active Listening' AI Marketing</a>\n   863→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   864→                    </div>\n   865→                    <div class=\"item-description\">FTC requires Cox Media Group and two other firms to pay nearly $1 million to settle charges they deceived customers about an 'Active Listening' AI-powered marketing service.</div>\n   866→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   867→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-22</span>\n   868→                    </div>\n   869→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   870→                        <span class=\"tag\">privacy</span>\n   871→                        <span class=\"tag\">ftc</span>\n   872→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   873→                    </div>\n   874→                </div>\n   875→\n   876→                <div class=\"item\">\n   877→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   878→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/memory-shortage/\" target=\"_blank\">Memory shortage causing repricing of consumer electronics</a>\n   879→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n   880→                    </div>\n   881→                    <div class=\"item-description\">David Oks explains why consumer products using memory will get more expensive. Memory manufacturers have fixed wafer capacity split between DDR, LPDDR, and HBM.</div>\n   882→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   883→                        <span class=\"author\">David Oks</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-22</span>\n   884→                    </div>\n   885→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   886→                        <span class=\"tag\">memory</span>\n   887→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   888→                        <span class=\"tag\">hardware</span>\n   889→                    </div>\n   890→                </div>\n   891→\n   892→                <div class=\"item\">\n   893→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   894→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/21/datasette-agent/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent - extensible AI assistant for Datasette</a>\n   895→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   896→                    </div>\n   897→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon announced the first release of Datasette Agent, a new extensible AI assistant for Datasette. After working on his LLM Python library for just over three years.</div>\n   898→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   899→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-21</span>\n   900→                    </div>\n   901→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   902→                        <span class=\"tag\">sqlite</span>\n   903→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   904→                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n   905→                    </div>\n   906→                </div>\n   907→\n   908→                <div class=\"item\">\n   909→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   910→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/20/spacex-anthropic-deal/\" target=\"_blank\">SpaceX S-1: Anthropic paying $1.25B/month for compute</a>\n   911→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   912→                    </div>\n   913→                    <div class=\"item-description\">SpaceX filing reveals Cloud Services Agreements with Anthropic for access to compute capacity across COLOSSUS and COLOSSUS II. Anthropic agreed to pay $1.25 billion per month.</div>\n   914→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   915→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-20</span>\n   916→                    </div>\n   917→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   918→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   919→                        <span class=\"tag\">grok</span>\n   920→                        <span class=\"tag\">infrastructure</span>\n   921→                    </div>\n   922→                </div>\n   923→\n   924→                <div class=\"item\">\n   925→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   926→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/19/gemini-3.5-flash/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini 3.5 Flash: more expensive, but Google plan to use it for everything</a>\n   927→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-technical\">technical</span>\n   928→                    </div>\n   929→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Google released Gemini 3.5 Flash at Google I/O, skipping the preview modifier and going straight to general availability. Google appears to be using it for many key products.</div>\n   930→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   931→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-19</span>\n   932→                    </div>\n   933→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   934→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   935→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   936→                        <span class=\"tag\">gemini</span>\n   937→                    </div>\n   938→                </div>\n   939→\n   940→                <div class=\"item\">\n   941→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   942→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/19/six-months-llms-five-minutes/\" target=\"_blank\">The last six months in LLMs in five minutes</a>\n   943→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-tutorial\">tutorial</span>\n   944→                    </div>\n   945→                    <div class=\"item-description\">Simon's annotated slides from his five minute lightning talk at PyCon US 2026, covering major developments in LLMs over the previous six months.</div>\n   946→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   947→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-19</span>\n   948→                    </div>\n   949→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   950→                        <span class=\"tag\">lightning-talks</span>\n   951→                        <span class=\"tag\">pycon</span>\n   952→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   953→                    </div>\n   954→                </div>\n   955→\n   956→                <div class=\"item\">\n   957→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   958→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/17/gds-nhs-open-source/\" target=\"_blank\">GDS weighs in on the NHS's decision to retreat from Open Source</a>\n   959→                        <span class=\"type-badge type-opinion\">opinion</span>\n   960→                    </div>\n   961→                    <div class=\"item-description\">UK Government Digital Service published 'AI, open code and vulnerability risk in the public sector' recommending to keep open by default.</div>\n   962→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   963→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> · <span class=\"source\">Blog</span> · <span class=\"published-date\">2026-05-17</span>\n   964→                    </div>\n   965→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   966→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   967→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   968→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai</span>\n   969→                    </div>\n   970→                </div>\n   971→            </section>\n   972→        </div>\n   973→    </main>\n   974→\n   975→    <footer>\n   976→        <div class=\"container\">\n   977→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated on 2026-05-28</p>\n   978→            <p>\n   979→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n   980→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a> |\n   981→                <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n   982→            </p>\n   983→            <p style=\"margin-top: 10px; color: #999999;\">\n   984→                Inspired by Hacker News design principles\n   985→            </p>\n   986→        </div>\n   987→    </footer>\n   988→</body>\n   989→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
