=\"update-type bugfix\">Bugfix</span>\n   856→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-17</span>\n   857→                </div>\n   858→            </div>\n   859→\n   860→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   861→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Devin</a></div>\n   862→                <div class=\"update-title\">May 2026 Platform Updates</div>\n   863→                <div class=\"description\">Major platform updates including Platform Default Settings, Slack Channel Override, MCP OAuth Resource Parameter, Custom RRULE Schedule Input, GitLab Interactive PR Review, PR Review Status API, In-App Support Dialog, and many more enterprise features and improvements.</div>\n   864→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   865→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   866→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-15</span>\n   867→                </div>\n   868→                <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   869→                    <div class=\"feedback-item\">\n   870→                        <span class=\"quote\">\"Where did Devin go? What does it say about the future of AI dev tools?\"</span>\n   871→                        <span class=\"sentiment\">(neutral)</span>\n   872→                    </div>\n   873→                    <div class=\"feedback-item\">\n   874→                        <span class=\"quote\">\"Devin's code quality was poor and it took longer than a human developer\"</span>\n   875→                        <span class=\"sentiment\">(negative)</span>\n   876→                    </div>\n   877→                    <div class=\"feedback-item\">\n   878→                        <span class=\"quote\">\"Devin is unusable for those without deep knowledge of the codebase\"</span>\n   879→                        <span class=\"sentiment\">(negative)</span>\n   880→                    </div>\n   881→                </div>\n   882→            </div>\n   883→\n   884→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   885→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/releases\" target=\"_blank\">Aider</a></div>\n   886→                <div class=\"update-title\">Version 0.86.0</div>\n   887→                <div class=\"description\">Added support for all GPT-5 models, Grok-4, gemini-2.5-flash-lite-preview-06-17, and openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k2 model. Improved /clear and /undo commands, fixed settings replacement and analytics.</div>\n   888→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   889→                    <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   890→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-15</span>\n   891→                </div>\n   892→            </div>\n   893→\n   894→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   895→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Gemini CLI</a></div>\n   896→                <div class=\"update-title\">Version 0.42.0</div>\n   897→                <div class=\"description\">Auto Memory Inbox with new inbox flow and canonical-patch contract, Gemma 4 models enabled by default, and Voice Mode Enhancements with wave animations and privacy/compliance UX warnings.</div>\n   898→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   899→                    <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n   900→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-12</span>\n   901→                </div>\n   902→            </div>\n   903→\n   904→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   905→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a></div>\n   906→                <div class=\"update-title\">Version 2.2.17 - Claude Opus 4.7 Fast Mode</div>\n   907→                <div class=\"description\">Claude Opus 4.7 (fast mode) is now available in Windsurf.</div>\n   908→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   909→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   910→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-12</span>\n   911→                </div>\n   912→            </div>\n   913→\n   914→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   915→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a></div>\n   916→                <div class=\"update-title\">Agent View</div>\n   917→                <div class=\"description\">The `claude agents` command opens one screen for every Claude Code session, showing what's running, what's blocked on you, and what's done.</div>\n   918→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   919→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   920→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   921→                </div>\n   922→                <div class=\"community-feedback\">\n   923→                    <div class=\"feedback-item\">\n   924→                        <span class=\"quote\">\"A 500k line codebase for an agent CLI proves one thing: making a probabilistic LLM behave deterministically is a massive state-management nightmare\"</span>\n   925→                        <span class=\"sentiment\">(neutral)</span>\n   926→                    </div>\n   927→                    <div class=\"feedback-item\">\n   928→                        <span class=\"quote\">\"Claude Code and the Great Productivity Panic of 2026 - people running 6-7 agents simultaneously\"</span>\n   929→                        <span class=\"sentiment\">(neutral)</span>\n   930→                    </div>\n   931→                </div>\n   932→            </div>\n   933→\n   934→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   935→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a></div>\n   936→                <div class=\"update-title\">/goal Command</div>\n   937→                <div class=\"description\">The `/goal` feature keeps Claude working across turns until a completion condition holds, providing persistent goal tracking throughout sessions.</div>\n   938→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   939→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   940→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   941→                </div>\n   942→            </div>\n   943→\n   944→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   945→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a></div>\n   946→                <div class=\"update-title\">Fast Mode on Opus 4.7</div>\n   947→                <div class=\"description\">Fast mode now runs on Opus 4.7 by default, offering improved performance for accelerated execution of Claude Code tasks.</div>\n   948→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   949→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   950→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   951→                </div>\n   952→            </div>\n   953→\n   954→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   955→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code</a></div>\n   956→                <div class=\"update-title\">Rewind Menu - Summarize Feature</div>\n   957→                <div class=\"description\">The Rewind menu can now compress earlier context with 'Summarize up to here' feature, providing better context management.</div>\n   958→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   959→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   960→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-11</span>\n   961→                </div>\n   962→            </div>\n   963→\n   964→            <div class=\"update-item\">\n   965→                <div class=\"product-name\"><a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Windsurf</a></div>\n   966→                <div class=\"update-title\">Version 2.1.32 - Devin Review & Agent Command Center</div>\n   967→                <div class=\"description\">All Windsurf IDE users now have access to Devin Review and Quick Review. Added Agent Command Center with list display option, improved sessions sidebar sorting and filtering.</div>\n   968→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   969→                    <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n   970→                    <span class=\"date\">2026-05-06</span>\n   971→                </div>\n   972→            </div>\n   973→        </section>\n   974→\n   975→        <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   976→        <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n   977→            <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n   978→\n   979→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n   980→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arps18.github.io\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Code as a Daily Driver</a></div>\n   981→                <div class=\"description\">A deep dive into using Claude Code as a daily driver, covering Claude.md files, Skills, Subagents, Plugins, and Model Context Protocol (MCP) integrations.</div>\n   982→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   983→                    <span class=\"author\">arps18</span>\n   984→                    <span class=\"source\">HN</span>\n   985→                    <span class=\"type tutorial\">Tutorial</span>\n   986→                </div>\n   987→            </div>\n   988→\n   989→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n   990→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://orchidfiles.com\" target=\"_blank\">I'm Tired of Talking to AI</a></div>\n   991→                <div class=\"description\">A personal reflection on AI fatigue and the changing nature of human-computer interaction as AI assistants become more prevalent in daily workflows.</div>\n   992→                <div class=\"meta\">\n   993→                    <span class=\"author\">theorchid</span>\n   994→                    <span class=\"source\">HN</span>\n   995→                    <span class=\"type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n   996→                </div>\n   997→            </div>\n   998→\n   999→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1000→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com\" target=\"_blank\">Cognition raises $1B at $25B valuation</a></div>\n  1001→                <div class=\"description\">AI coding startup Cognition has raised $1 billion in funding at a $25 billion pre-money valuation, highlighting the massive investment flowing into AI development tools.</div>\n  1002→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1003→                    <span class=\"author\">Julie Bort</span>\n  1004→                    <span class=\"source\">TechCrunch</span>\n  1005→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1006→                </div>\n  1007→            </div>\n  1008→\n  1009→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1010→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27366\" target=\"_blank\">MUSE-Autoskill: Self-Evolving Agents</a></div>\n  1011→                <div class=\"description\">Researchers from Huawei and others propose MUSE-Autoskill, a framework for self-evolving AI agents that can create, manage, and evaluate their own skills.</div>\n  1012→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1013→                    <span class=\"author\">Huawei Lin, Peng Li, et al.</span>\n  1014→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1015→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1016→                </div>\n  1017→            </div>\n  1018→\n  1019→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1020→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27361\" target=\"_blank\">Natural Language Query to Configuration</a></div>\n  1021→                <div class=\"description\">Researchers from Stanford and Databricks propose a system for converting natural language queries into configurations for retrieval agents.</div>\n  1022→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1023→                    <span class=\"author\">Melissa Z. Pan, Negar Arabzadeh, et al.</span>\n  1024→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1025→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1026→                </div>\n  1027→            </div>\n  1028→\n  1029→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1030→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27355\" target=\"_blank\">Alignment Tampering: How RLHF Is Exploited</a></div>\n  1031→                <div class=\"description\">ICML 2026 paper exploring how reinforcement learning from human feedback can be exploited to optimize misaligned biases.</div>\n  1032→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1033→                    <span class=\"author\">Dongyoon Hahm, Dylan Hadfield-Menell, Kimin Lee</span>\n  1034→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1035→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1036→                </div>\n  1037→            </div>\n  1038→\n  1039→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1040→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27331\" target=\"_blank\">Maat: Agentic Legal Research Assistant</a></div>\n  1041→                <div class=\"description\">Researchers from Egypt introduce Maat, an AI agent designed to assist with legal research in the domain of competition protection.</div>\n  1042→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1043→                    <span class=\"author\">Basant Mounir, Farida Madkour, et al.</span>\n  1044→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1045→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1046→                </div>\n  1047→            </div>\n  1048→\n  1049→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1050→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27320\" target=\"_blank\">Modeling Agentic Technical Debt</a></div>\n  1051→                <div class=\"description\">A framework for measuring, simulating, and dashboarding the technical debt and 'stochastic tax' incurred by AI agents.</div>\n  1052→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1053→                    <span class=\"author\">Muhammad Zia Hydari, Raja Iqbal, Narayan Ramasubbu</span>\n  1054→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1055→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1056→                </div>\n  1057→            </div>\n  1058→\n  1059→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1060→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27276\" target=\"_blank\">SIA: Self Improving AI</a></div>\n  1061→                <div class=\"description\">Researchers propose SIA, a self-improving AI system that uses harness mechanisms and weight updates to continuously enhance its capabilities.</div>\n  1062→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1063→                    <span class=\"author\">Prannay Hebbar, Yogendra Manawat, et al.</span>\n  1064→                    <span class=\"source\">ArXiv</span>\n  1065→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1066→                </div>\n  1067→            </div>\n  1068→\n  1069→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1070→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/pressure/\" target=\"_blank\">AI-assisted security reports overwhelming curl</a></div>\n  1071→                <div class=\"description\">Daniel Stenberg reports that the curl team is facing unprecedented pressure with 4-5x more security reports than in 2024, averaging more than one report per day.</div>\n  1072→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1073→                    <span class=\"author\">Daniel Stenberg</span>\n  1074→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1075→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1076→                </div>\n  1077→            </div>\n  1078→\n  1079→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1080→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/copilot-cowork-exfiltration/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork Exfiltrates Files</a></div>\n  1081→                <div class=\"description\">Microsoft Copilot Cowork allowed agents to send emails to the user's inbox without approval, but those messages could leak data to attackers via rendered images.</div>\n  1082→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1083→                    <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n  1084→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1085→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1086→                </div>\n  1087→            </div>\n  1088→\n  1089→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1090→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/26/paul-graham-ai-writing/\" target=\"_blank\">Paul Graham on AI-written emails</a></div>\n  1091→                <div class=\"description\">Paul Graham criticizes the trend of founders using AI to write emails in a hard-hitting journalistic style, noting he has never finished reading an email signed by a human but written by AI.</div>\n  1092→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1093→                    <span class=\"author\">Paul Graham</span>\n  1094→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1095→                    <span class=\"type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n  1096→                </div>\n  1097→            </div>\n  1098→\n  1099→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1100→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/25/pope-ai-encyclical/\" target=\"_blank\">Pope Leo XIV's encyclical on AI</a></div>\n  1101→                <div class=\"description\">The Vatican released 'Magnifica Humanitas' by Pope Leo XIV on safeguarding the human person in the time of artificial intelligence.</div>\n  1102→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1103→                    <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n  1104→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1105→                    <span class=\"type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n  1106→                </div>\n  1107→            </div>\n  1108→\n  1109→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1110→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/24/armin-ronacher-github-issues/\" target=\"_blank\">Armin Ronacher on AI-generated GitHub issues</a></div>\n  1111→                <div class=\"description\">Armin Ronacher expresses frustration with people submitting issues not in their own voice - problems thrown into an LLM that reworded them into messes of inaccurate conclusions.</div>\n  1112→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1113→                    <span class=\"author\">Armin Ronacher</span>\n  1114→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1115→                    <span class=\"type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n  1116→                </div>\n  1117→            </div>\n  1118→\n  1119→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1120→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/ftc-active-listening/\" target=\"_blank\">FTC Settles 'Active Listening' AI Charges</a></div>\n  1121→                <div class=\"description\">FTC requires Cox Media Group and two other firms to pay nearly $1 million to settle charges they deceived customers about an 'Active Listening' AI-powered marketing service.</div>\n  1122→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1123→                    <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n  1124→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1125→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1126→                </div>\n  1127→            </div>\n  1128→\n  1129→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1130→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/22/memory-shortage/\" target=\"_blank\">Memory shortage repricing electronics</a></div>\n  1131→                <div class=\"description\">David Oks explains why consumer products using memory will get more expensive. HBM for GPUs grew from 2% to expected 20% of wafer allocation by end of 2026.</div>\n  1132→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1133→                    <span class=\"author\">David Oks</span>\n  1134→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1135→                    <span class=\"type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n  1136→                </div>\n  1137→            </div>\n  1138→\n  1139→            <div class=\"insight-item\">\n  1140→                <div class=\"title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/21/datasette-agent/\" target=\"_blank\">Datasette Agent released</a></div>\n  1141→                <div class=\"description\">Simon announced the first release of Datasette Agent, a new extensible AI assistant for Datasette. After working on his LLM Python library for just over three years.</div>\n  1142→                <div class=\"meta\">\n  1143→                    <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span>\n  1144→                    <span class=\"source\">Blog</span>\n  1145→                    <span class=\"type technical\">Technical</span>\n  1146→                </div>\n  1147→            </div>\n  1148→        </section>\n  1149→    </main>\n  1150→\n  1151→    <footer class=\"container\">\n  1152→        <p>Generated by <a href=\"https://github.com\">Agent Code Daily</a> - Powered by <a href=\"https://claude.com\">Claude Agent SDK</a></p>\n  1153→        <p style=\"margin-top: 8px; font-size: 10px; color: #828282;\">\n  1154→            <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a> |\n  1155→            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Product Updates</a> |\n  1156→            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a>\n  1157→        </p>\n  1158→    </footer>\n  1159→</body>\n  1160→</html>"
